1
00:00:01,325 --> 00:00:06,080
I still remember how shocked I was.

2
00:00:07,211 --> 00:00:09,760
There was no warning at all,

3
00:00:10,365 --> 00:00:12,262
and the reality was so cruel.

4
00:00:18,788 --> 00:00:21,897
The warm hands that used to pat my head…

5
00:00:23,760 --> 00:00:28,194
The kind smile that used to heal my heart…

6
00:00:28,857 --> 00:00:34,571
He was stronger, kinder, and
more diligent than anyone…

7
00:00:35,291 --> 00:00:37,965
And even he couldn't achieve his dreams?

8
00:00:38,697 --> 00:00:40,640
It made no sense.

9
00:00:41,611 --> 00:00:44,045
Of course I felt some guilt.

10
00:00:45,622 --> 00:00:46,594
But still…

11
00:00:47,026 --> 00:00:47,737
[Ayanokoji Kiyotaka]

12
00:00:47,820 --> 00:00:49,407
[Ayanokoji Kiyotaka]
I couldn't forgive that man.

13
00:00:49,490 --> 00:00:50,047
[Ayanokoji Kiyotaka]

14
00:00:50,130 --> 00:00:51,771
[Ayanokoji Kiyotaka]
If it meant taking him down,

15
00:00:52,342 --> 00:00:56,320
I would harden my soft heart,

16
00:00:57,314 --> 00:01:01,120
and work towards my true goal.

17
00:02:34,251 --> 00:02:35,969
What a view!

18
00:02:36,052 --> 00:02:36,367
[An Ominous Opening]
What a view!

19
00:02:36,450 --> 00:02:37,554
[An Ominous Opening]
Did you not see it last year?

20
00:02:37,637 --> 00:02:38,594
Did you not see it last year?

21
00:02:38,902 --> 00:02:41,360
Well, I did see a little of it,

22
00:02:41,531 --> 00:02:45,245
but was too focused on having fun
with my friends to appreciate it.

23
00:02:46,697 --> 00:02:49,428
It still kinda doesn't feel real.

24
00:02:49,611 --> 00:02:53,074
It's not that often you get to go
on a cruise, after all.

25
00:02:53,737 --> 00:02:55,474
That's not what I meant.

26
00:02:55,611 --> 00:02:58,125
I meant going out with you.

27
00:02:58,571 --> 00:03:01,782
You never pick up on these things.

28
00:03:02,434 --> 00:03:04,605
So, how's it for you?

29
00:03:04,891 --> 00:03:07,234
Does it feel real for you yet?

30
00:03:08,114 --> 00:03:10,297
I'm… not sure.

31
00:03:10,731 --> 00:03:14,400
It both does and doesn't.

32
00:03:14,548 --> 00:03:16,114
The heck does that mean?

33
00:03:16,308 --> 00:03:21,531
Well, I never imagined being able to meet
outside without anybody seeing us.

34
00:03:21,885 --> 00:03:23,348
There is that, I guess.

35
00:03:23,794 --> 00:03:27,394
Depending on the details they
announce for the exam,

36
00:03:27,611 --> 00:03:30,080
I may have to ask you for a favor.

37
00:03:30,525 --> 00:03:32,171
I get that.

38
00:03:32,548 --> 00:03:35,474
And I'll do it if I can.

39
00:03:37,760 --> 00:03:39,988
Looks like the first-years are done.

40
00:03:40,502 --> 00:03:43,771
We can't be seen together,
so I'll head over first.

41
00:03:52,754 --> 00:03:54,937
Why would you sit here?!

42
00:03:55,074 --> 00:03:57,097
Are you doing this on purpose?!

43
00:03:57,245 --> 00:03:58,377
Completely.

44
00:03:58,662 --> 00:04:01,017
Ugh, why should I have to mov…

45
00:04:03,428 --> 00:04:07,531
I will now explain the rules for the
deserted island special exam.

46
00:04:07,920 --> 00:04:13,154
Starting tomorrow, for two weeks, you will
compete for points in a survival exam.

47
00:04:13,611 --> 00:04:16,057
Emptied groups are eliminated,

48
00:04:16,524 --> 00:04:19,497
and the five lowest-scoring
groups will be expelled.

49
00:04:19,760 --> 00:04:22,171
There are two ways to earn points.

50
00:04:22,377 --> 00:04:23,954
The first is basic movement.

51
00:04:24,102 --> 00:04:28,537
The island is split into a 100-cell grid.
Move to specified cells for points.

52
00:04:29,020 --> 00:04:33,200
Four cells will be specified per day,
announced at fixed times.

53
00:04:33,805 --> 00:04:38,537
Rules govern these. Three per day will be
within two cells cardinally

54
00:04:38,697 --> 00:04:41,200
or one cell diagonally from the last.

55
00:04:41,554 --> 00:04:45,097
But, once per day, a cell
will be chosen randomly,

56
00:04:45,302 --> 00:04:47,188
so you can make no predictions.

57
00:04:47,630 --> 00:04:54,011
The first group to arrive will get ten points,
the second five, the third three,

58
00:04:54,251 --> 00:04:59,017
and all who arrive in time will
receive one bonus point.

59
00:04:59,337 --> 00:05:04,102
but a group's arrival time is determined
by when the full group is present.

60
00:05:04,582 --> 00:05:08,925
And if your group happens to already be
in a cell when it is specified,

61
00:05:09,257 --> 00:05:12,674
you will get one point, but not
this Early Bird bonus.

62
00:05:13,131 --> 00:05:17,451
Failure to arrive in three specified
cells in a row will be penalized.

63
00:05:17,885 --> 00:05:21,074
Before I explain the other
method of earning points,

64
00:05:21,245 --> 00:05:22,720
take a look at this.

65
00:05:23,554 --> 00:05:26,754
We will have you wear these watches
until the exam is over,

66
00:05:26,960 --> 00:05:29,771
and distribute linked
tablets to each of you.

67
00:05:29,977 --> 00:05:34,354
These will be essential tools that
determine your point awards.

68
00:05:34,811 --> 00:05:38,411
We will be monitoring
your health at all times,

69
00:05:38,651 --> 00:05:40,674
and if your vitals cross a set line,

70
00:05:40,937 --> 00:05:42,822
a warning alarm will sound.

71
00:05:43,862 --> 00:05:46,697
It is set to stop after five seconds,

72
00:05:46,925 --> 00:05:51,017
but if you remain over
the line, it will repeat.

73
00:05:52,034 --> 00:05:53,748
If this continues,

74
00:05:54,308 --> 00:05:56,388
it will change to an emergency alert.

75
00:05:56,868 --> 00:06:00,880
In this case, you are to undergo a medical
checkup at the starting zone,

76
00:06:01,280 --> 00:06:03,417
but if you cannot reach it,

77
00:06:03,577 --> 00:06:06,308
you will drop out and may be penalized.

78
00:06:06,868 --> 00:06:09,851
If your emergency alert stays
active for five minutes,

79
00:06:10,045 --> 00:06:13,474
the teaching and medical staff will
rush to your GPS location.

80
00:06:13,780 --> 00:06:19,988
Naturally, forcible removal and equipment
malfunctions will disable point gains.

81
00:06:20,754 --> 00:06:24,125
You must exchange your watch for
a new one at the start zone.

82
00:06:24,651 --> 00:06:26,697
Now, let's return to basic movement.

83
00:06:27,120 --> 00:06:31,622
During the exam, groups will not
all be moving to the same areas.

84
00:06:32,137 --> 00:06:35,462
These watches contain
twelve different tables.

85
00:06:35,988 --> 00:06:40,697
Your table will determine all of your
specified cells from start to finish.

86
00:06:41,440 --> 00:06:44,662
Naturally, all members of a group
will be on the same table,

87
00:06:44,845 --> 00:06:48,582
and if you form a large group, you
will all switch to the same table.

88
00:06:49,165 --> 00:06:54,765
The second method of earning points is completing
tasks set around the island.

89
00:06:55,531 --> 00:06:58,685
The tasks' locations and content
cannot be predicted.

90
00:06:59,040 --> 00:07:01,417
You can view their
participation conditions,

91
00:07:01,565 --> 00:07:05,394
but you must make your way
to them to learn their contents.

92
00:07:06,000 --> 00:07:09,748
Completing a task can reward
you with food or water.

93
00:07:10,057 --> 00:07:14,217
Groups will be approved if they
link their watches.

94
00:07:15,554 --> 00:07:20,708
Now, Acting Director Tsukishiro has
his own speech to give you.

95
00:07:26,411 --> 00:07:28,057
Tsukishiro here.

96
00:07:28,240 --> 00:07:34,000
This deserted island exam is of an
unprecedentedly large scale.

97
00:07:35,062 --> 00:07:39,942
I would like to give you all just
one word of warning.

98
00:07:40,640 --> 00:07:43,508
In its role as your guardian here,

99
00:07:43,702 --> 00:07:46,468
the school will maintain
maximum surveillance.

100
00:07:46,925 --> 00:07:51,920
But that does not mean its vision
extends across the entire island.

101
00:07:52,320 --> 00:07:57,382
Sexual troublemakers will be
penalized without hesitation,

102
00:07:57,588 --> 00:08:01,645
and we will report any
crimes to the police.

103
00:08:02,548 --> 00:08:04,262
And one more thing.

104
00:08:04,594 --> 00:08:08,651
There may be some who become frustrated
over a lack of food or water,

105
00:08:08,811 --> 00:08:11,462
causing scuffles with other students.

106
00:08:12,342 --> 00:08:17,931
To a certain extent, I
intend to allow this.

107
00:08:18,422 --> 00:08:23,120
This is because it is impossible
to entirely prevent strife.

108
00:08:23,405 --> 00:08:28,731
Of course, if the line of criminality is
crossed, the school will intervene.

109
00:08:29,040 --> 00:08:30,502
Depending on circumstances,

110
00:08:30,800 --> 00:08:35,062
you may be dropped from the
exam, or even expelled.

111
00:08:35,965 --> 00:08:37,679
That is all.

112
00:08:37,965 --> 00:08:44,708
I ask that you please act as befits Advanced
Nurturing High School students.

113
00:08:48,114 --> 00:08:51,280
[Advanced Nurturing High School Deserted Island
Special Exam] Thank you, Acting Director Tsukishiro.

114
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:53,638
Now, for our last topic, we will move on
to essential food and tools.

115
00:08:53,721 --> 00:08:58,721
[Deserted Island Survival Set] Now, for our last
topic, we will move on to essential food and tools.

116
00:09:01,497 --> 00:09:04,465
Whoa, look at all that!

117
00:09:04,548 --> 00:09:06,468
Is this really enough for everyone?

118
00:09:06,857 --> 00:09:08,571
Wh-What?!

119
00:09:08,662 --> 00:09:12,411
How to put it? I guess we both
have difficult personalities.

120
00:09:12,800 --> 00:09:14,991
It's not easy to join the rabble.

121
00:09:15,074 --> 00:09:17,051
Huh?! Don't lump me in with you!

122
00:09:17,200 --> 00:09:18,571
I can do it just fine.

123
00:09:22,548 --> 00:09:24,087
What are you doing?

124
00:09:24,170 --> 00:09:24,170
What are you doing?
I thought I'd get… all the water… we'd need.

125
00:09:24,253 --> 00:09:31,704
I thought I'd get… all
the water… we'd need.

126
00:09:33,462 --> 00:09:35,348
Potable water is precious,

127
00:09:35,702 --> 00:09:40,880
but it seems I'll have to either find it
on-site or earn it from tasks.

128
00:09:55,234 --> 00:09:56,937
How'd you sleep last night?

129
00:09:59,988 --> 00:10:01,565
Normally.

130
00:10:01,817 --> 00:10:04,274
You're not feeling sick, are you?

131
00:10:04,537 --> 00:10:07,462
Still holding last year against me?

132
00:10:07,737 --> 00:10:10,102
No, just teasing you.

133
00:10:10,537 --> 00:10:14,891
The special exam is starting,
yet you seem rather relaxed.

134
00:10:15,154 --> 00:10:17,725
Panicking won't change anything.

135
00:10:19,473 --> 00:10:20,977
[Time until next area announcement
Time to reach area Target area]

136
00:10:21,060 --> 00:10:22,457
Mine's F9.

137
00:10:22,994 --> 00:10:25,085
Looks like we're on different tables.

138
00:10:25,760 --> 00:10:28,468
I won't be worrying about you anymore.

139
00:10:28,868 --> 00:10:31,142
Just get a high rank, even on your own.

140
00:10:31,565 --> 00:10:33,542
I'd like to,

141
00:10:33,817 --> 00:10:37,760
but it won't be funny if I end up
being the only one expelled.

142
00:10:38,160 --> 00:10:40,274
That would be a problem, yes.

143
00:10:40,948 --> 00:10:44,011
I just lent you some points, after all.

144
00:10:44,354 --> 00:10:45,680
That's your issue?

145
00:10:46,228 --> 00:10:50,685
I can't blame you for being low on funds,
given your contract with Kushida,

146
00:10:50,937 --> 00:10:54,422
but giving up half your points
every month is too much.

147
00:10:54,880 --> 00:10:56,742
I'm all too aware of that.

148
00:10:57,108 --> 00:11:02,240
Don't push yourself too hard. This will
be really hard for a girl on her own.

149
00:11:02,434 --> 00:11:05,165
I'll just take that as
a bit of kind advice.

150
00:11:06,057 --> 00:11:08,685
None of the second-year
groups are in a rush.

151
00:11:09,040 --> 00:11:12,662
The first-years got more than
ten minutes' head start.

152
00:11:13,005 --> 00:11:17,851
Wasting stamina racing for the first
area would be a poor strategy.

153
00:11:20,731 --> 00:11:24,754
Is Koenji seriously aiming to take first?

154
00:11:24,891 --> 00:11:28,285
Beats me. We made a bet, yes,

155
00:11:28,468 --> 00:11:31,771
but I have no idea how
he'll try to handle it.

156
00:11:32,480 --> 00:11:35,154
Promises are non-binding, after all.

157
00:11:35,462 --> 00:11:39,531
Alriiiight! Let's go get number one!

158
00:11:39,862 --> 00:11:42,868
Hurry it up, Nishino! You too, Tsube!

159
00:11:42,994 --> 00:11:46,068
It's too hot. Don't ask the impossible.

160
00:11:46,434 --> 00:11:49,737
Besides, it's too late
to beat the firsties.

161
00:11:50,125 --> 00:11:52,445
When you give up, it's all over!

162
00:11:52,788 --> 00:11:55,954
Who knows! The firsties
might be taking it easy!

163
00:11:56,125 --> 00:11:59,531
Give it a rest! It'd just
be a waste of stamina.

164
00:11:59,657 --> 00:12:01,497
Or, hey, just go it alone.

165
00:12:01,580 --> 00:12:06,902
But then we wouldn't get the Early Bird bonus,
and it'd be a pain to regroup!

166
00:12:07,828 --> 00:12:08,777
There you are!

167
00:12:11,954 --> 00:12:13,234
Need something?

168
00:12:13,337 --> 00:12:14,982
Not in particular.

169
00:12:15,268 --> 00:12:16,582
Just to tell you…

170
00:12:17,028 --> 00:12:18,788
I'm not going to lose. Ever.

171
00:12:21,565 --> 00:12:24,765
Does she even understand how
hard this exam will be?

172
00:12:24,971 --> 00:12:27,737
She seems incredibly motivated, at least.

173
00:12:28,137 --> 00:12:30,297
Having a rival is a good thing.

174
00:12:30,617 --> 00:12:33,108
Not that I view her as one.

175
00:12:33,554 --> 00:12:36,948
If nothing else, I'm relieved
we're on different tables.

176
00:12:37,862 --> 00:12:38,891
And now…

177
00:12:39,622 --> 00:12:41,371
It's time I got going.

178
00:12:54,114 --> 00:13:00,525
One of the points of this exam is to avoid
missing any designated cells.

179
00:13:01,348 --> 00:13:07,497
Early Bird bonuses and high placement in tasks
can get you five or ten points,

180
00:13:07,771 --> 00:13:11,714
but that takes a lot of
skills, smarts, and luck.

181
00:13:12,285 --> 00:13:16,742
As such, getting one point at a time,
every time, will be crucial.

182
00:13:18,137 --> 00:13:20,617
Are you discussing the next area?

183
00:13:21,142 --> 00:13:22,651
Oh, Kiyopon.

184
00:13:23,005 --> 00:13:26,388
Our first area was here, in D8.

185
00:13:26,582 --> 00:13:28,320
We're already done.

186
00:13:28,617 --> 00:13:30,354
Where are you headed, Kiyotaka?

187
00:13:30,537 --> 00:13:32,491
D7, one cell north.

188
00:13:32,731 --> 00:13:36,754
We could have stayed together if only
we were on the same table.

189
00:13:36,902 --> 00:13:38,548
Well, there are twelve.

190
00:13:38,742 --> 00:13:41,988
Anyway, I'm going to get going to my area.

191
00:13:42,148 --> 00:13:46,845
It's a bit sad to part, so I hope we
can find time to chat longer!

192
00:13:47,748 --> 00:13:51,268
There are a lot of ways to
cooperate across groups,

193
00:13:52,194 --> 00:13:53,020
Take care!
- but if they have members that'd hold me back,

194
00:13:53,103 --> 00:13:56,114
but if they have members
that'd hold me back,

195
00:13:56,274 --> 00:13:58,320
I have to avoid them.

196
00:13:59,154 --> 00:14:02,685
I'm lucky we're on
different tables this time.

197
00:14:09,314 --> 00:14:14,182
I should head for the center of the cell,
to be ready to go any direction.

198
00:14:15,737 --> 00:14:18,548
If I want to determine
who else is on my table,

199
00:14:18,731 --> 00:14:21,142
my only option is direct observation.

200
00:14:21,451 --> 00:14:22,788
Good morning.

201
00:14:23,302 --> 00:14:26,617
Nanase. Where are Hosen and Amasawa?

202
00:14:26,811 --> 00:14:28,788
Investigating the area.

203
00:14:29,394 --> 00:14:34,240
I decided to come here to see how
many other groups there are.

204
00:14:34,582 --> 00:14:36,445
The same as me, then.

205
00:14:37,085 --> 00:14:41,337
I expect you'll have your share of
troubles on your own. Take care.

206
00:14:41,782 --> 00:14:43,337
Excuse me.

207
00:14:46,262 --> 00:14:49,565
Three hours until the
next area gets announced.

208
00:14:50,582 --> 00:14:54,697
So it's either wait, or go for a task.

209
00:14:59,417 --> 00:15:02,000
Hey there, Ayanokoji!

210
00:15:02,262 --> 00:15:05,417
So you came here? Too bad, though.

211
00:15:05,805 --> 00:15:08,891
The deadline was five minutes ago.

212
00:15:09,120 --> 00:15:11,071
So it seems.

213
00:15:11,154 --> 00:15:13,588
You don't have to be in such a hurry.

214
00:15:13,725 --> 00:15:15,645
You're allowed to spectate.

215
00:15:15,920 --> 00:15:21,451
I think it's problematic when teachers
try to steal students' time.

216
00:15:21,634 --> 00:15:24,411
Aww, that's a bit harsh, don't you think?

217
00:15:24,537 --> 00:15:28,365
I just wanted to chat a little!

218
00:15:29,417 --> 00:15:33,577
We haven't talked like this since
the closing ceremony.

219
00:15:33,714 --> 00:15:34,937
We haven't.

220
00:15:35,097 --> 00:15:38,457
And yet you've gotten all
kinds of attention since.

221
00:15:38,697 --> 00:15:41,645
And here I thought you
didn't like to stand out.

222
00:15:41,794 --> 00:15:43,360
I don't.

223
00:15:43,634 --> 00:15:47,862
Then why did you get a
perfect score in math?

224
00:15:47,988 --> 00:15:50,400
That seems pretty outstanding to me.

225
00:15:50,708 --> 00:15:56,354
I'm pretty sure plenty of students could
have answered problems like those.

226
00:15:56,468 --> 00:15:59,222
You think so? I wonder.

227
00:15:59,405 --> 00:16:03,062
Even if they could, you're in Class D.

228
00:16:03,280 --> 00:16:09,497
You sure it's a good idea to acknowledge
someone with crazy high specs is in it?

229
00:16:09,691 --> 00:16:14,297
I think 2-D has plenty of
remarkable students in it.

230
00:16:14,468 --> 00:16:16,514
1-D does, too.

231
00:16:17,600 --> 00:16:19,622
That's true, but…

232
00:16:20,148 --> 00:16:24,582
The school's really
changed since last year.

233
00:16:26,205 --> 00:16:28,902
Yes, I believe there
are remarkable students,

234
00:16:29,177 --> 00:16:32,754
but not enough to move a
whole class, or rather,

235
00:16:32,937 --> 00:16:37,497
none that give the impression they're
changing anything, like you do.

236
00:16:37,794 --> 00:16:42,834
So she's gathering information in
places I can't see, is she?

237
00:16:43,337 --> 00:16:46,628
I'm in a bit of a bind, myself.

238
00:16:46,880 --> 00:16:49,771
I've never been dropped to Class C before,

239
00:16:49,965 --> 00:16:53,920
and here I thought this
class could reach A.

240
00:16:54,194 --> 00:16:57,497
And you think it should fall
to someone else to fix that?

241
00:16:58,125 --> 00:17:00,137
That's a low blow.

242
00:17:01,200 --> 00:17:03,920
Hey, I just had a groundbreaking idea!

243
00:17:04,130 --> 00:17:09,428
You could join my class, like how
Katsuragi transferred to Class B!

244
00:17:09,680 --> 00:17:12,228
That's a hell of a thing to say.

245
00:17:12,387 --> 00:17:15,348
You can shoot for Class
A with us! How about it?

246
00:17:15,724 --> 00:17:20,696
I can't get twenty million points
before graduation.

247
00:17:21,061 --> 00:17:26,079
Besides, we don't yet know which class
will win its way to A in the end.

248
00:17:26,411 --> 00:17:29,885
Y-You didn't have to take it so seriously…

249
00:17:32,480 --> 00:17:35,611
Sudo's changed a lot, too.

250
00:17:36,125 --> 00:17:37,931
Who changed him, hm?

251
00:17:38,685 --> 00:17:41,451
Just for the record, it wasn't me.

252
00:17:41,748 --> 00:17:44,171
Anyway, I'll be heading back now.

253
00:17:45,234 --> 00:17:49,611
They'll be stationing me here and
there throughout the exam,

254
00:17:49,702 --> 00:17:51,428
so we might meet again!

255
00:17:57,085 --> 00:17:58,422
Ayanokoji.

256
00:17:58,914 --> 00:18:00,194
That's twice today.

257
00:18:00,560 --> 00:18:02,651
It is. What a coincidence.

258
00:18:03,051 --> 00:18:04,651
How'd today go for you?

259
00:18:05,028 --> 00:18:08,525
It was all I could do to get three
points from arrival bonuses.

260
00:18:08,891 --> 00:18:09,828
And you?

261
00:18:10,217 --> 00:18:16,308
We got eight points from arrivals, and took
first in a task for 13 points in all.

262
00:18:16,697 --> 00:18:18,708
Sounds like you took off running.

263
00:18:18,857 --> 00:18:19,782
We did.

264
00:18:20,251 --> 00:18:21,097
Um…

265
00:18:22,068 --> 00:18:23,851
No, it's nothing.

266
00:18:29,645 --> 00:18:36,537
Even if Tsukishiro wants to get me expelled
by forcing me into the bottom five,

267
00:18:37,017 --> 00:18:39,622
I'm in charge of my point earnings.

268
00:18:40,091 --> 00:18:43,462
Which means he could manipulate
my watch or tablet,

269
00:18:43,668 --> 00:18:47,337
showing me false target destinations,

270
00:18:48,228 --> 00:18:50,834
but if I complained to the school,

271
00:18:51,028 --> 00:18:53,302
that half-baked strategy would fail.

272
00:18:55,668 --> 00:18:58,148
If he's using a White Room student,

273
00:18:58,365 --> 00:19:01,760
they'd try to force me out
due to injury or illness.

274
00:19:02,411 --> 00:19:07,497
Which means they'd attack
when I'm in a blind spot.

275
00:19:08,662 --> 00:19:11,634
That's the most realistic
method of expelling me.

276
00:19:22,182 --> 00:19:24,308
E8, huh?

277
00:19:34,468 --> 00:19:38,228
Considering the travel time,
I should let this one pass.

278
00:19:44,365 --> 00:19:50,091
Second twice in a row. I might have
a formidable rival on this table.

279
00:19:50,845 --> 00:19:53,302
Guess I'll go back to
E6 and wait for a task.

280
00:19:58,297 --> 00:19:59,897
Ayanokoji.

281
00:20:00,800 --> 00:20:06,331
We meet again. Do you think we
might be on the same table?

282
00:20:06,754 --> 00:20:07,840
Possibly.

283
00:20:08,834 --> 00:20:11,074
Even if we head for the same areas,

284
00:20:11,360 --> 00:20:14,342
our chances of meeting aren't that high.

285
00:20:14,765 --> 00:20:17,817
This could just be a string
of coincidences, but…

286
00:20:18,628 --> 00:20:21,920
Um, if you don't mind,
I have a favor to ask.

287
00:20:22,194 --> 00:20:23,291
Such as?

288
00:20:24,057 --> 00:20:28,594
If it's not an imposition, could we
stick together for a while?

289
00:20:29,314 --> 00:20:31,942
Stick together? What's this about?

290
00:20:32,320 --> 00:20:38,240
The truth is, last night Hosen and Amasawa
said they'd go their own ways,

291
00:20:38,468 --> 00:20:40,354
so we've gotten split up.

292
00:20:40,708 --> 00:20:43,474
That could be considered a strategy.

293
00:20:43,942 --> 00:20:48,765
I don't believe I can reach the designated
areas very quickly on my own.

294
00:20:49,245 --> 00:20:53,851
Meanwhile, I've run into you three
times since yesterday morning,

295
00:20:54,080 --> 00:20:57,954
and with just one exception,
you reached the areas first.

296
00:20:58,365 --> 00:21:03,714
I can't say it's wise for groups to
cooperate across school years.

297
00:21:04,091 --> 00:21:07,302
If you reach a task that only has
room for one more group,

298
00:21:07,531 --> 00:21:09,942
an argument is guaranteed to ensue.

299
00:21:10,525 --> 00:21:13,942
I don't mind letting you take
priority for all of them.

300
00:21:14,400 --> 00:21:17,862
That'll naturally result in your
point income decreasing.

301
00:21:18,102 --> 00:21:21,051
This is my first deserted island exam,

302
00:21:21,348 --> 00:21:25,817
so even having suitable routes
picked for me is a huge help.

303
00:21:26,182 --> 00:21:29,497
Even if I did pick suitable routes,

304
00:21:29,657 --> 00:21:31,714
could you keep up with me?

305
00:21:32,605 --> 00:21:34,902
I'm confident in my stamina.

306
00:21:35,314 --> 00:21:39,017
Or is it less that it's a bother,
and more you don't trust me?

307
00:21:40,822 --> 00:21:44,960
Got it. If that's what
you want, I don't mind.

308
00:21:45,211 --> 00:21:46,742
Thank you very much.

309
00:21:47,405 --> 00:21:52,114
What are your plans now? We have over
an hour before the next announcement.

310
00:21:52,411 --> 00:21:57,405
A quiz task appeared in F8, to the
southeast. I'm going there.

311
00:21:57,794 --> 00:22:00,400
Got it. I'll come with.
